# Change Log
All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.
 
The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](http://keepachangelog.com/)
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](http://semver.org/).
 
## [Unreleased] - yyyy-mm-dd
 
Here we write upgrading notes for brands. It's a team effort to make them as
straightforward as possible.

### Breaking
- BREAKING: database env vars renamed from `SQL_*` to `DB_*`
  - `SQL_HOST` -> `DB_HOST`
  - `SQL_PORT` -> `DB_PORT`
  - `SQL_DATABASE_NAME` -> `DB_NAME`
  - `SQL_USERNAME` -> `DB_USERNAME`
  - `SQL_PASSWORD` -> `DB_PASSWORD`
  - `SQL_DIALECT` -> `DB_DIALECT`
  - `SQL_MAX_POOL` -> `DB_MAX_POOL`
  - `SQL_MIN_POOL` -> `DB_MIN_POOL`
  - `SQL_IDLE` -> `DB_IDLE`

### Added
- TypeScript (`strict`): `src/` and `tests/` are `.ts`, typed Sequelize models, `tsc` build to `dist/`, `typecheck` script
- Jest and supertest: unit tests and integration tests (auth, user, role) against Postgres, `npm test` / `npm run test:coverage`, `docker-compose.yml` for the test database and a GitHub Actions workflow
- `POST /v1/auth/refresh-tokens` ([#2](https://github.com/japananh/node-express-postgres-boilerplate/issues/2))
- `SQL_PORT` environment variable
- Migration `add-role-constraints`: foreign key `user.role_id` -> `role.id` and unique `role.name`, as in the removed flyway baseline. **Upgrade note:** it fails if existing rows already violate them (duplicate role names, users with an unknown role)
- `.nvmrc` (Node 26)

### Changed
- `DELETE /v1/roles/:roleId` answers 409 while users still have the role; `PATCH`/`POST /v1/roles` answer 409 for a duplicate name
- The demo user seeder is renamed (`20210227144500-demo-user`) so `db:seed:all` seeds the role first
- `npm start` runs the compiled `dist/index.js`; `npm run dev` uses `tsx watch` instead of nodemon
- ESLint uses `@typescript-eslint` (ESLint 8, `eslint-config-airbnb-base` 15); tests run through `ts-jest`
- Require Node >= 26 (`.nvmrc` 26); bump `jsonwebtoken` to 9 and `express-jwt` to 8 (Node 25+ removed `SlowBuffer`, which the old `jsonwebtoken` needs), `sequelize` to 6.37 and `prettier` to 2.8
- Remove the stray `package-lock.json` (v1, only held the `update-changelog` deps; `yarn.lock` is the lockfile)
- Remove the unused `flyway/` folder ([#1](https://github.com/japananh/node-express-postgres-boilerplate/issues/1)); the schema lives in the Sequelize migrations

### Fixed
- Unauthenticated requests returned 500 instead of 401
- `DELETE /v1/roles/:roleId` returned 500 (missing `deleteRoleById`)
- Login with an unknown email returned 500 instead of 401
- `POST /v1/auth/reset-password` returned 500 for an invalid token and accepted access tokens
- `sequelize-cli` ignored `SQL_USERNAME` and used the OS user
- Demo role seeder violated `modified_date_time NOT NULL`
- `PATCH /v1/roles/:roleId` returned 200 with an empty body for a missing role (now 404), and did not validate its body or id (400 for an empty body, unknown fields or a non-numeric id); `DELETE /v1/roles/:roleId` rejects a non-numeric id with 400
- `GET`, `PATCH` and `DELETE /v1/users/:userId` returned 500 for a non-numeric or out-of-range id (now 400)
- Swagger documented `role` where the API takes `roleId` (register, user queries) and returns `role_id`

